---
title: Home
permalink: /
---
<main class="main-style">
    <div id="index-body" class="body-style">
        <div id="hero-section" class="section-div flex flex-col min-h-screen relative">
            {# <div id="photo" class="inline-block w-auto mb-8 md:mb-12">
                <img src="/assets/images/dipesh2.webp" alt=""
                    class="w-60 h-60 mx-auto object-cover rounded-4xl">
            </div> #}
            <div id="intro" class="mt-48 md:mt-96 mb-8">
                <div class="text-xl md:-mb-2 font-medium 
                            dark:text-darkaccent2-200 text-accent2-500">
                    Hi there! I'm
                </div>
                <div class="page-title-font-style font-bold text-6xl xl:text-8xl -ml-1 
                          dark:text-fill-300 text-accent2-300">Dipesh Kumar</div>
                <h3 class="text-left font-header md:max-w-3xl lg:max-w-4xl text-2xl md:text-5xl font-medium 
                        dark:text-darkaccent2-500 text-fill-500">
                    Software Developer by day and night.
                </h3>
                <h4 class="text-left text-lg mt-8 md:max-w-3xl lg:max-w-4xl
                        dark:text-darkaccent1-50 text-accent1-50">
                    I specialize in crafting modern desktop experiences within the Windows ecosystem 
                    (WPF/WinUI), focusing on robust UI toolkits that feel as good as they look. While,
                    I enjoy developing components to aid UI developers, I'm currently expanding my horizon
                    in the world of distributed systems and scalable architectures.
                </h4>
            </div>
            {# <div>
                <a href="https://drive.google.com/file/d/1AFSSzhv9SuvjyP-Am3ukRk6_0hB40fKG/view?usp=sharing" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" 
                class="font-bold my-4 link">
                    Resume
                </a>
            </div> #}

            <div id="socials" class="flex flex-row flex-wrap items-center -ml-4 mt-16 mb-4 lg:mb-0">
                {% for social in info.socials %}
                    <span class="mx-4">
                        <a href="{{ social.url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="link">
                            <i class="{{ social.icon }} fa-lg"></i>
                        </a>
                    </span>
                {% endfor %}
            </div>
        </div>

        <div id="about-section" class="section-div section-spacing">
            <h2 class="section-heading md:mb-8">About Me</h2>
            <p class="text-left dark:text-darkaccent2-50 text-accent1-500">
                Hello and welcome! I'm Dipesh Kumar, a spirited Software Developer 
                II at Microsoft, where I contribute on maintaining WPF's robustness 
                and introducing new innovative features.
                <br>
                <br>
                In my software journey, I've developed a strong knack for backend REST 
                development and have honed my skills in the Angular and Django frameworks. 
                I'm deeply fascinated by the realms of data structures, algorithms, 
                system design, and architecture - areas where I continually seek to 
                expand my expertise. My professional curiosity also extends into 
                the field of Natural Language Processing, a domain where 
                I've engaged in multiple stimulating projects.
                <br>
                <br>
                When I am not working, one will find me immersed in 
                making designs, editing photos and reading. Currently, 
                I'm reading <span class="font-semibold"><i>Do It Today</i></span>. 
                Among my other recent reads, I really enjoyed 
                <span class="font-semibold"><i>1984</i></span> by G. Orwell and 
                <span class="font-semibold"><i>The Lost Symbol</i></span> by Dan Brown.
                Beyond my professional pursuits, I'm an avid lover of tea and coffee 
                - the perfect companions for both code and contemplation. 
                My love for adventure often takes me on hiking trails and road trips, 
                experiences that I cherish and share in the gallery on this website.
                <br>
                <br>
                Over the years, I have worked with various different technologies and languages.
                Some for personal projects, wherease others on a more official capacity. Some of
                them include:
                <br>
                <br>
            </p>
            <div id="skills-list" class="flex flex-wrap flex-row mx-0">
                {% for skill in info.skills %}
                    <span class="rounded-2xl pr-2 py-1 mt-1 text-left dark:font-medium font-bold
                                text-accent2-300 dark:text-darkaccent1-500" >
                        {{ skill.name }}
                    </span>
                    <span class="last:hidden text-accent2-300 dark:text-darkaccent1-500 py-1 pr-2 mb-1">.</span>
                {% endfor %}
            </div>
        </div>

        <div id="work-section" class="section-div section-spacing">
            <h2 class="section-heading md:mb-8 text-right">Experience</h2>
            <p class="text-left text-accent1-500 dark:text-darkaccent2-50">
                Major portion of my professional journey has revolved around development
                of Desktop UI Frameworks for Windows ecosystem, shifting gears from WPF to
                WinUI in the last year. Even though, core principles guiding my work remain
                the same in this domain, but after working on variety of issues and features
                and complex problems, I have developed a muscle when it comes to both UI and
                UI Framework development.
            </p>

            <div id="experience-list" class="flex flex-col w-10/12 mt-12 mx-auto">
                {% for exp in info.experiences %}
                    <div class="grid grid-cols-4 gap-4 mb-6">
                        <h5 class="col-start-1 font-bold dark:font-medium text-fill-500 dark:text-fill-50 text-left text-sm m-1"> 
                            <span>{{ exp.time | makeUppercase }}</span>
                        </h5>
                        <h5 class="col-start-2 col-span-3 font-semibold text-xl
                                    text-accent2-500 dark:text-darkaccent2-300 *:inline-block" >
                            <span class="">{{ exp.role }}</span> 
                            <span class="mx-1"> &#x2022; </span>
                            <span class="">{{ exp.company }}</span>
                        </h5>
                        <ul class="col-start-2 col-span-3 text-md text-accent1-500 dark:text-darkaccent2-50 list-disc">
                            {% for expitem in exp.details %}
                                <li class="mb-4 last:mb-0">{{ expitem }}</li>
                            {% endfor %}
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                {% endfor %}
            </div>
        </div>    
        
        <div id="projects-section" class="section-div">
            <div id="projects-heading" class="mb-8 md:mb-16">
                <h2 class="section-heading md:mb-8">Projects</h2>
                <p class="text-left text-accent1-500 dark:text-darkaccent2-50">
                    In my professional journey, I've tackled a wide range of projects, 
                    from simple web apps to complex database management systems. 
                    Each one has offered unique challenges and learning opportunities. 
                    Below are some of the most intriguing projects I've worked on. 
                    For a complete overview of my projects, visit the Projects page.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div id="projects-list" class="flex flex-wrap justify-center flex-col mx-auto
                                            md:gap-x-6 text-left w-10/12 md:w-full xl:w-10/12">
                {% for selected_project in info.selectedprojects %}
                    {% for project in collections.Project %}
                        {% if project.data.post_slug == selected_project %}
                            <div id="{{ project.post_slug }}-project-card" 
                                class="mb-8 md:mb-16 
                                       flex flex-row even:flex-row-reverse
                                       odd:[&>div:last-child]:-ml-32 even:[&>div:last-child]:-mr-32">
                                <div class="image-wrapper w-96 h-72 group">
                                    <div class="h-full w-96 overflow-clip rounded-sm">
                                        <img src="/assets/images/{{ project.data.post_image }}" alt=""
                                            class="h-full w-full filter object-cover
                                                   grayscale group-hover:grayscale-0  
                                                   transition duration-300" />
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="image-overlay rounded-sm
                                                transition duration-300"></div>
                                </div>

                                <div class="rounded-sm z-10 max-h-56 my-auto w-full p-8
                                            dark:bg-accent2-500 bg-accent2-500 shadow-xl/30">
                                    <div class="flex sm:flex-col flex-row justify-between">
                                        <span class="font-bold text-xl pr-2
                                                        dark:text-fill-50 text-darkaccent2-50">{{ project.data.title }}</span>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="mt-4 min-h-8 max-h-32">
                                        <span class="text-sm dark:text-darkaccent2-50 text-fill-50">{{ project.data.description }}</span>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        {% endif %}
                    {% endfor %}
                {% endfor %}
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</main>
